(7034343, 1067508, 83366, '<td valign="top">Thanks a lot for your comments ! It''s been taken from my iPhone with a little of post processing... I added the original picture in the description.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Paul:</b></div><hr/><i> This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 9s - I like it a lot. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: <br/> <br/>1. Great focus and depth of field - perfectly judged for the scene.<br/> <br/>2. Excellent exposure and wide latitude tones - again perfectly judged, we see all but have sufficient contrast.<br/> <br/>3. Extraordinarily cute child, bright, aware and seemingly well but with the juxtaposition of what appears to be a hospital context conspires to communicate a compelling story.<br/> <br/>4. The through-the-bars shot is bold, it offers some distance and introduces some order that eradicates sentimentality - a bold choice given the subject matter.<br/> <br/>Overall, conveys the compelling matter-of-factness I''ve enjoyed in <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=133611" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">nick_hinch</a>''s work. I wonder who shot this one...? </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks a lot for your comments ! It''s been taken from my iPhone with a little of post processing... I added the original picture in the description. Originally posted by Paul: This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 9s - I like it a lot. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:  1. Great focus and depth of field - perfectly judged for the scene. 2. Excellent exposure and wide latitude tones - again perfectly judged, we see all but have sufficient contrast. 3. Extraordinarily cute child, bright, aware and seemingly well but with the juxtaposition of what appears to be a hospital context conspires to communicate a compelling story. 4. The through-the-bars shot is bold, it offers some distance and introduces some order that eradicates sentimentality - a bold choice given the subject matter. Overall, conveys the compelling matter-of-factness I''ve enjoyed in  nick_hinch''s work. I wonder who shot this one...? ', '2013-05-08 08:13:51.000000', NULL, 0),
