(7034443, 1065241, 80831, '<td valign="top">Nothing special really.  This was taken in Red Rock park in Sedona, Az.  There was a bathroom door of all things open behind me that lit up the barn and tree really nicely.  All I did was setup the camera on the tripod, set focus to infinity, ISO 2000 or 2500, 20 sec, F 2.8 ...i believe were the settings...just happened to get really lucky with the shooting star.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RyanW:</b></div><hr/><i> would love to know your steps to get this image. the night sky is simply beautiful. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Nothing special really.  This was taken in Red Rock park in Sedona, Az.  There was a bathroom door of all things open behind me that lit up the barn and tree really nicely.  All I did was setup the camera on the tripod, set focus to infinity, ISO 2000 or 2500, 20 sec, F 2.8 ...i believe were the settings...just happened to get really lucky with the shooting star. Originally posted by RyanW: would love to know your steps to get this image. the night sky is simply beautiful. ', '2013-05-08 12:37:08.000000', NULL, 0),
